  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Ryan Billingsley said banks are increasingly using AI and machine learning for fraud detection, AML/CFT processes, and credit underwriting, and are testing generative AI for tasks such as answering customer questions and summarizing loan applicant information. He said it is essential to enable banks to adopt AI and other technologies while maintaining expectations that they manage associated risks and operate safely and soundly. He said the FDIC is piloting generative AI for internal staff use and expects to roll those tools out to its workforce by the middle of the year. He said the FDIC is investing in workforce training that covers AI literacy, generative AI concepts, AI governance, critical evaluation of AI outputs, and human oversight.",
   "sids": [
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s1",
    "s4",
    "s5",
    "s6",
    "s7"
   ],
